01:15:18.730 --> 01:15:38.600
Steve McCown (Anonyome Labs, Inc.): It's all written in legalese. What's interesting about this is Utah is creating a new type of digital identity that is very, user-centric. The idea is that we want users to… we want to acknowledge that users, individuals own their identity, not the state.

646
01:15:38.640 --> 01:15:57.339
Steve McCown (Anonyome Labs, Inc.): So this is something that's presented by the individual to the state for endorsement, and not given by the state to the individual. And that seems… when I describe it to people, like the birth certificate process, that's, it resonates pretty well. But…

647
01:15:57.410 --> 01:16:03.389
Steve McCown (Anonyome Labs, Inc.): Typically, legislation, state and country laws don't, don't look at it that way.

