01:18:15.840 --> 01:18:27.440
Steve McCown (Anonyome Labs, Inc.): will have to support SETI in its systems. And so, by hitting some of those areas, there's a path to wide-scale adoption.

660
01:18:27.690 --> 01:18:41.600
Steve McCown (Anonyome Labs, Inc.): So people wanting to purchase, you know, vapes or cigarettes or whatever at the convenience store, they will have to, if they want to present a digital identity, it should be this one.

661
01:18:41.930 --> 01:18:51.070
Steve McCown (Anonyome Labs, Inc.): Other things that are in there, there's a duty of loyalty. Think of that as terms of service. So you share your identity, your name, your email, your phone number.

662
01:18:51.240 --> 01:18:55.700
Steve McCown (Anonyome Labs, Inc.): Think of it like terms of service you're giving to the verifier.

663
01:18:55.940 --> 01:19:11.549
Steve McCown (Anonyome Labs, Inc.): That they can use that for the terms you've agreed on, to make the sale, to send you information, but they can't sell that identity information the way they've been doing, kind of, wholesale.

664
01:19:11.630 --> 01:19:20.750
Steve McCown (Anonyome Labs, Inc.): And so the duty of Loyalty talks about how your data will be used when it's provided under, using a SETI.

